{"title":"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine all three-digit numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> having the property that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is divisible by 11, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132ce2db8ef5687cb88489944664e1d99448a2f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{N}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> is equal to the sum of the squares of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/c/c1c6c366e931cb9eed2a345eb9f9eff66d213ce5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N = 100a + 10b+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"156\" height=\"14\" /> for some digits <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/b/f3b28547efd22be1c4a05fa193cd7038fc65d71b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"29\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/2/f1290e6e100fc16188bc4b670ad244f670a79ba5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[100a + 10b+c = 11m\\]\" width=\"171\" height=\"14\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. We also have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/0/b90d0cd1e138b2f02f26dc88acd3562c0d9a8e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m=a^2+b^2+c^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"131\" height=\"16\" />. Substituting this into the first equation and simplification, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/1/ca12dd1191538f2338a2597e454d71c0562120df.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[100a+10b+c = 11a^2 +11b^2 +11c^2\\]\" width=\"283\" height=\"16\" /> For an integer divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, the the sum of digits in the odd positions minus the sum of digits in the even positions is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Thus we get: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/0/490434efdfeae2b3b14b63a92b6c85d6b80835c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = a + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da54597e808152730e47322ca070a43a46b2ac3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = a + c - 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Case <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52a8a5642f9d10fb23dcec02ac8f898b8936252.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=a+c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"72\" height=\"14\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/b/f7b22665294fde26249cc95236e9bad8b2233b0c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[100a+c+10a+10c = 11a^2 +11c^2+11(a+c)^2\\]\" width=\"379\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/4/a0405b565d5c5622e122197e0d6bf23a04c10257.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10a+c = 2a^2+2ac+2c^2\\]\" width=\"201\" height=\"17\" /> Since the right side is even, the left side must also be even. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/1/241e24df5ea12c3af03305f1feb451cd4ea87c83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=2q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/4/ed4fc191364e338c98969cc1296d65075516d223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q = 0,1,2,3,4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/7/0c77fc67040c2e8df93ee8129916df995e61ddb2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10a+2q=2a^2+4aq+8q^2\\]\" width=\"212\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/9/fa94744b5ce0ff91aafc92f94e00144c6ffc01b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[5a+q=a^2+2aq+4q^2\\]\" width=\"186\" height=\"18\" /> \nSubstitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/66550be1c7d977114b04db1e645ee71085a15980.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=0,1,2,3,4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"16\" /> into the last equation and then solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. \n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/6/8062318143377fad82aa5171b3efedf615871972.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"16\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/8/53897e4b47f6049266b4bffcef91bc949385b5e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80d7a3ca845e6cae14b9db710b64331219ec3f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f69c1ec597d19324140f3130e9d63367f4b69c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b=5$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />. We get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c944a2993690dfc2bb5f8dd5f822f18463661d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=550$\" width=\"67\" height=\"12\" /> which works.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/26520f2333a3d48eb4929b7517dea54293f36605.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not an integer. There is no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> for this case. \n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/2/4/2249017892bda0490d89aa6d997b953b070b1ba1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"41\" height=\"15\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not an integer. There is no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> for this case.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a99bb04a5525117c5f4322d6886c384021a05ecc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"17\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not an integer. There is no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> for this case.\n</p><p>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/8/d08fda03bd2794c52d97ee08e0cccfe18b6859a0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, we get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not an integer. There is no <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> for this case.\n</p><p><br />\nCase <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />: Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/a/3da54597e808152730e47322ca070a43a46b2ac3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = a + c - 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" />. We get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/4/7f45d9282f849709ae7e04b0a5c9f29287a9692e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[100a+c+10a+10c -110= 11(a^2+(a+c)^2-22(a+c)+c^2+121)\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"19\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/33843b3e3d01279f941cf680929c5af5ed1504f5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[10a+c=2a^2+2c^2+2ac-22a-22c+131\\]\" width=\"349\" height=\"16\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b6ca1f3e226f02f09db2a295fcbe62504b498c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(a-8)^2+2(c-\\frac{23}{4})^2+2ac-\\frac{505}{8}=0\\]\" width=\"311\" height=\"38\" />\nNow we test all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/503153a5c1ca240258c37d326b7de930b32ba186.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=0\\rightarrow10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"87\" height=\"13\" />. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/b/a8be166c2ea97b29ea80433c2a6568973e640435.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=0,1,2,4,5,6,7,8,9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"180\" height=\"17\" />, we get no integer solution to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. Thus, for these values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />, there is no valid <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. However, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/7/8271d4342b38d2ab38bb626ffad8b9dae00b5e2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c=3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, we get  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be90bc0b7b8d38c002906c288b99b5e3a944462f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(a-8)^2+2(3-\\frac{23}{4})^2+6a-\\frac{505}{8}=0\\]\" width=\"304\" height=\"38\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/0/2008d95ea49fe2ab9b87dac5068d1f4473390bbd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(a-8)^2+6a-48 = 0\\]\" width=\"185\" height=\"19\" /> We get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/a/c1a0caf28dae25372408593f2d14ca238035568c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=8$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> is a valid solution. For this case, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/8/d484a39574fa89291b7281eb5fec8394b7b6a32c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=8,b=0,c=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"141\" height=\"16\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/5/8e50e71ce32ce63d134ccd984b8898e3d79a0303.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=803$\" width=\"67\" height=\"12\" />, and this is a valid value. Thus, the answers are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7d882610db3ce1fd0932cdbc8f720fee1a8e89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{N=550,803}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"115\" height=\"27\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Define a <b>ten</b> to be all ten positive integers which begin with a fixed tens digit.\n</p><p>We can make a systematic approach to this:\n</p><p><br />\nBy inspection, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132ce2db8ef5687cb88489944664e1d99448a2f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{N}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" /> must be between 10 and 90 inclusive. That gives us 8 tens to check, and 90 as well.\n</p><p>For a given ten, the sum of the squares of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> increases faster than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/2/132ce2db8ef5687cb88489944664e1d99448a2f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{N}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"38\" />, so we can have at most one number in every ten that works.\n</p><p>We check the first ten:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/e/4ae517c73f933669d86ee0b7764aed65dc14fea6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11*11=121$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/c/24c7adc55f63f6bca8ad38dbe94b6d7c2de03aae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2+2^2+1^2=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"127\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/b/8db39929393155e3d2b5d02cc75fd0ff832b8928.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12*11=132$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/8/078dd25f64ca20b5e02ae61591462cbdae514ae1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1^2+3^2+2^2=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>11 is too small and 12 is too large, so all numbers below 11 will be too small and all numbers above 12 will be too large, so no numbers in the first ten work.\n</p><p>We try the second ten:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/a/d5a2de31c70b6f65979f41768fd97ebf56ae7f34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21*11=231$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/d/f1d7a837e2052691a10fbb2b72a9e9660ea06722.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2+3^2+1^2=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/a/cda25b230701ec306c0239aaccc30f9204a3b5c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$22*11=242$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"104\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95c300deab1e4a64c4aa04a12182b97f9ebe9037.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^2+4^2+2^2=24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"136\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, no numbers in the second ten work.\n</p><p>We continue, to find out that 50 and 73 are the only ones that works.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/5/1b5a8e47ff1406c0f89e3025411b1ae33a0fbf7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=50*11=550$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"145\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/d/38d921a1a1f1db17915f8cad103cd412f9b51aa7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N=73*11=803$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"145\" height=\"13\" /> so there are two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> that works.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Note that there are only 900 three-digit numbers. Of these, only 81 are divisible by 11. This brings to mind the great strategy of listing and bashing. Being organized while listing will get you the answer. There is plenty of time on the IMO, and listing is highly unlikely to miss cases. We end up getting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/7/8c7d882610db3ce1fd0932cdbc8f720fee1a8e89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{N=550,803}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -9px\" width=\"115\" height=\"27\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c6h54826p22231968\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c6h54826p22231968</a>\n</p><p><br />\n~franzliszt\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/d/fcd37cc5f16a18df6880fbaf875ffc34d87d105d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N/11 = 10x + y, 0 \\leq x,y &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"241\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/f/f6fa751d929795dfd579fbf0c4a803eb11a7643a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y &lt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> then the squares of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> equals\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aed50ec6cdf230c1ead1beffe2eca0f7b72fc7b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 + (x+y)^2 + y^2 = 10x + y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"230\" height=\"21\" />. Simplifying, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2def10c5d3c39c7086609b363b42f2ec9d6f09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 + x(y-5) + y^2 - y/2 = 0.\\]\" width=\"231\" height=\"20\" />\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/0/5f09ab3a5541f584bfd368b1406921e502793aa8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 | y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"20\" />. This has discriminant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/58100d3cde6039869ff7d2d38e2b380c59d09e1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-3y^2-8y + 25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/b/3abe507e9eeeaec583f610e45b64dc4436cd3361.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> the discriminant is negative, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/2/2a261b71b48ceea8803ceaba56f60c3e75657df5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y&lt;2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec89f09c84538ec43930ca5d8e5e0957e2000822.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> we see x = 5. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/8/d7837835d5d11f86ac0805f3bf96f31d47fd39b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot xy = 11 \\cdot 50 = 550$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"17\" /> is a possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Alternatively, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/f/afffb414bb10e3b9faa6efbc2a769c931b018e14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+y \\geq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"86\" height=\"17\" /> then the squares of the digits of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> equals \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/7/4074da92213b8e4872015cc1695f9c0a20d917a5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x+1)^2 + (x+y-10)^2 + y^2 = 10x + y.\\]\" width=\"315\" height=\"20\" />\nSimplifying, we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/1/681841fd96bdc6237a506cdab55c74b7480bf20b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^2 + x(y-14) + y^2 + \\frac{101-21y}{2} = 0.\\]\" width=\"293\" height=\"37\" />\nSo <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/c/3eca709ea9e00f35c1f66398f4378d1f4dad362b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\nmid y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" />. This has discriminant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/6/c2650bae29fac4be17009c60b30fed8f47fcbfc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-6 + 14y - 3y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/3/2f34741131b4b0a78cb3cff04fcecc205ac291d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y \\geq 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> the discriminant is negative, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/b/71be91b3e156f48a845d59d43c4d2a8a168d76f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &lt; 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/4/234b330118777aba0bee513e3ade547ebd70d845.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> the discriminant equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3b4834614e5e7e189cb7d621cfb4fb0bd36dd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> is not a solution. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b0e1404de4eca35c42876bcc83707b753e990e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"45\" height=\"17\" /> the discriminant equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the quadratic equation implies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/8/b28f2e0a22768ad5146aa4df77699c95d48e6e34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = (11 \\pm 3)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"118\" height=\"20\" />. Since we assumed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/d/58d08229f2b9f788621097b22c6ceaca164aedac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x + y \\geq 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"16\" /> only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d1e7375e601943b3bb958a24e41da8920d601a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 7$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> is a solution. So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/0/ef07232d514d1035ebd95174427e8b2a6af9e064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11 \\cdot xy = 11 \\cdot 73 = 803$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"178\" height=\"17\" /> is a possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LB2KTsnnmSQ&amp;list=PLa8j0YHOYQQJGzkvK2Sm00zrh0aIQnof8&amp;index=2\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LB2KTsnnmSQ&amp;list=PLa8j0YHOYQQJGzkvK2Sm00zrh0aIQnof8&amp;index=2</a>\n- AMBRIGGS\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DRii5VjLk70\">https://youtu.be/DRii5VjLk70</a> [Video Solution]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO\" title=\"1960 IMO\">1960 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1960_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1960 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017143131\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.049 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.096 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 570/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 743/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 56/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18395/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   43.459      1 Template:IMO7_box\n100.00%   43.459      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:5669:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017143131 and revision id 277084. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}